# Code owners for dot-agent-deck.
#
# Scoped deliberately: review is required only on the surfaces where a mistake
# breaks interoperability between an older and a newer build — the TUI<->daemon
# protocol, the daemon itself, orchestration, and hooks. That is the same
# surface CLAUDE.md rule 12 already singles out for the cross-version contract
# check. Docs, tests, chores and the changelog merge without a code-owner
# approval so routine work keeps its current speed.
#
# NOTE ON SEQUENCING: a code owner cannot approve their own pull request. While
# @vfarcic is the only entry here, enabling "require review from Code Owners"
# would block every one of his PRs with nobody able to approve them. Do not turn
# that rule on until a second maintainer is listed below.

# --- Cross-version contract surface (CLAUDE.md rule 12) ---
/src/daemon.rs              @vfarcic
/src/daemon_protocol.rs     @vfarcic
/src/daemon_attach.rs       @vfarcic
/src/daemon_client.rs       @vfarcic
/src/daemon_stop.rs         @vfarcic
/src/hook.rs                @vfarcic
/src/hooks_manage.rs        @vfarcic
/src/codex_hooks_manage.rs  @vfarcic
/src/devin_hooks_manage.rs  @vfarcic
/src/orchestrator_ext.rs    @vfarcic

# --- Release and governance machinery ---
/.github/workflows/         @vfarcic
/.github/CODEOWNERS         @vfarcic
/scripts/                   @vfarcic

# When a second maintainer is onboarded (see docs/develop/governance.md),
# add them to every line above so that either maintainer can review the other.
# Until then the lines are documentation, not an enforced gate.
